  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/loricaria_simillima_en/",
      "html": "<ul><li>Total length: 25 cm</li><li>Water: medium hard</li><li>Omnivore</li><li>Mouthbrooder; the male guards the eggs and larvae</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/loricaria_simillima_en/",
      "html": "<p>Loricaria simillima has a very wide distribution in South America. It is found in the Orinoco, Amazon and La Plata basins. Origin: central South America.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/loricaria_simillima_en/",
      "html": "<p>As a result of this large range, many different colour forms are known, which differ clearly in coloration and pattern. The species occurs in different water types.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/loricaria_simillima_en/",
      "html": "<p>With a total length of 25 cm they should be kept in not too small tanks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/loricaria_simillima_en/",
      "html": "<p>Medium-hard water with a pH of 6–8 and temperatures between 24 and 27°C is sufficient. Blackwater forms are more demanding in maintenance and breeding than fish originating from white water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/loricaria_simillima_en/",
      "html": "<p>The aquarium should have a sandy substrate; some dark corners made with stones and bogwood increase the fish's comfort.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/loricaria_simillima_en/",
      "html": "<p>As omnivorous fish they are rather undemanding in their nutrition; tablet food, flakes and frozen food are accepted.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/loricaria_simillima_en/",
      "html": "<p>They are mouthbrooders; the male guards the eggs and larvae.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/loricaria_simillima_en/",
      "html": "<p>Loricaria comes from the Latin \"lorica\", the chest protector of a Roman legionnaire, i.e. \"one that wears a chest protector\". simillima is Latin for \"very similar\", referring to the similarity of the species to L. cataphracta.</p>"
    }
  ],
